      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "well, for random stuff like that you need a normal seeded random generator, restoring and syncing state sounds like weird hack.\nSo yea, expose system random. Also remember that methods like update might be called different time per second on each client anyways.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-01T18:23:59.534Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While trying to make a procedural generated map i encountered one fairly big problem when it came into syncing the generation.\nWhen you use a seed to have the UnityEngine.Random object to generate the same values for everyone you can get the desired effect only in the current frame, from the successive frame onwards it will generate values differently from each other. My guess is that UnityEngine.Random is also used internally by vrc for other stuff, and that causes the internal state of the random generator to desync.\nOne solution would be to store the state of the number generator at the end of the frame and reset it at the start of the next frame, but that needs the UnityEngine.Random.State class to be exposed.\nAnother solution would be to Expose the System.Random class instead, since that class is not static and you can instance indepenent objects that would also avoid potential interference of UnityEngine.Random being set and reset by the user and then vrc using it internally for other reasons consequentently alterning the random generation.",
